{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it was after these things.</b> From the day heaven and earth were created, no man would sneeze and survive his illness; rather, wherever he was — on the road or in the marketplace — if he sneezed, his soul would depart, until Jacob came and sought mercy for this. He said before HaKadosh Barukh Hu: Master of the universe, do not take my soul from me until I command my house — my sons and my grandsons. And he was answered, as it says: <b>and it was after these things</b>, etc. All the kings of the earth heard — they trembled and fell ill, for there had been none like it since the world was created. Therefore a person is obligated at the time of his sneeze to give thanks to HaKadosh Barukh Hu, who turned him from death to life, as it says: ״his sneezing flashes forth light.״ Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer. [ויאמר ליוסף — the verse is elliptical.]"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:59.400099928Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}